TEMPLATE FILES THE RENDERER LOOKS FOR (web/templates/)
  layout.html                    executed as template "layout.html"; calls {{template "content" .}}; may use {{block "head" .}}{{end}} / {{block "scripts" .}}{{end}}
  partials/*.html                all parsed into every set (so fragments can be rendered stand-alone)
  pages/{home,recipes_list,recipe_view,cook,recipe_edit,inbox_list,inbox_item,settings,tokens,admin_categories,signin,logged_out,error}.html
                                 each defines "content" (+ optional "head"/"scripts")
  Fragment template names (must exist in partials/ or the page file): results, favourite_button, visibility_control, cooklog_section, image_tile,
  upload_error, recipe_form, conflict (+ includes recipe_card, oven_hero, stage_card, delete_dialog, flash, language_button, category_chips, cooklog_entry, stars).
  A missing page file => HTTP 500 "template error: ..." in dev mode (visible in the browser).

CONTRACT NOTES / ADDITIONS (all additive; see docs/contract-questions.md for the reasoning)
  1. AMBIGUITY: Layout and RecipeBody both have Title/Lang/Dir. On RecipeView, CookView and InboxItemView, `.Title .Lang .Dir` are the
     RECIPE's values (methods). layout.html MUST read page/UI values as `.Layout.Lang`, `.Layout.Dir`, `.Layout.Title` (works for every view model).
  2. Layout.ClientI18n map[string]string (all js.* and oven.mode.* strings of the current language): render with
     <script type="application/json" id="client-i18n">{{.Layout.ClientI18n}}</script>.
  3. ImageView has an extra RecipeID (for image_tile). New funcs: add, sub, list (besides the 4.2 set). `url` errors loudly on unknown route names.
  4. JSON key names inside <script type=application/json> blocks: #editor-config = camelCase of the Go fields: mode, recipeId, userId, draftKey,
     version, action, signinUrl, suggestUrl, uploadUrl, orderUrl, deleteImageUrlTemplate (contains the literal `__ID__` to substitute), maxImages,
     maxImageBytes, maxStages. #cook-config = recipeId, userId, title, servings, stages:[{position,label,totalSeconds,stage1Seconds,isGourmet,preAlert,stage2Notice}]
     (stage2Notice is the stage-2 temperature like "140 °C"; the text around it comes from your js.* keys). #oven-spec = snake_case per contract 4.6
     (render with {{.OvenSpec}}).
  5. Other Go-generated values are plain strings: flash text is already localized; Layout.Title is the localized page title.
  6. Draft key (EditorConfig.DraftKey) is the full string `nwr_draft:<userId>:<recipeId|new|inbox:<id>>`.
  7. RecipeForm/StageForm fields are strings (input preserved); StageForm.Idx is "0".."9" or "__N__" for the <template>. Errors/Warnings maps are keyed by
     the form field name ("title", "stage[0].temperature_c", "category", "tags", "ingredients", "steps"); `fieldID` turns it into the DOM id.
  8. Language form: POST {{url "lang"}} with fields lang=<Layout.OtherLang> and return_to=<Layout.Path>.

i18n KEYS THAT GO CODE REFERENCES AND THE UI CATALOG (ui.en.toml / ui.he.toml) MUST DEFINE
  page titles: home.title list.title inbox.title settings.title tokens.title admin.title signin.title editor.new.title editor.edit.title editor.inbox.title
  list filters (Go builds the active-filter chips): list.filter.smoked  list.filter.favourites  list.filter.max_time ({{.Minutes}})  list.scope.mine  list.scope.family
  editor.save  editor.save_and_keep (EditorView.SubmitKey)
  error.<code>.title and error.<code>.body for codes: not_found forbidden bad_request conflict too_large unsupported_media internal unavailable not_allowed
  signin_failed signin_expired busy (ErrorView.Code)
  js.* (served to the client via Layout.ClientI18n; {name}-style placeholders).
  Backend-owned keys you MAY use: oven.mode.* oven.preset.* oven.pellet.* oven.accessory.* oven.frame.* unit.* time.* (time.h, time.min, time.s), flash.*,
  err.heic (the HEIC message), err.* , issue.* (already resolved into Errors/Warnings strings), app.name, app.version.

